course: dictionary
lesson: 6790
title: Orca: a word from the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An orca is a big animal that lives in the sea. You can use context to work out what a word means, and the words near it are its clues. Here the clue is «also called a killer whale», which tells you that orca and killer whale are two names for the same animal.
explain: The words «Orca groups are led by old grandmothers» give a clue about the word group. An orca group is a family, led by an older female who remembers where to find food. The lesson uses the word pod for this family group.
explain: Context clues also help when the word is a long name, like «humpback» or «echolocate». Read the sentence again and ask: what is it being compared to, and what does it do? Then check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: An orca is a large black-and-white sea mammal with a tall back fin.
fact: Orcas are also called killer whales, and they are the biggest members of the dolphin family.
fact: Orcas live and hunt in family groups called pods, in all the world's oceans, especially cold ones.
fact: Orcas breathe air through a blowhole on top of their head, and they feed their young milk.
fact: Toothed whales, like orcas, use echolocation, but baleen whales, like the blue whale, gulp tiny krill instead.
exercise: What is a pod? | *A family group of orcas that lives and hunts together | A kind of fish that orcas eat | A single orca swimming alone | A tall black fin on the back
exercise: «An orca, also called a killer whale, is a large sea mammal.» What do the words «also called» tell you? | A killer whale is a small fish | *The orca and the killer whale are the same animal | Orcas are not whales at all | Killer whales live only in lakes
exercise: «Toothed whales like dolphins, orcas and sperm whales echolocate.» Which of these is a toothed whale? | Krill | *Orca | Blue whale | Humpback
test: Orcas breathe air. How do they do it? | Through gills, like a fish | *Through a blowhole on top of their head | Through their tails | Through their mouths only
test: «Orca groups are led by old grandmothers who can live 80 or even 90 years.» How long can these grandmothers live? | 100 days | 8 years | *80 or even 90 years | 18 years
exam: Which word in «an orca, also called a killer whale» tells you the two names mean the same animal? | killer | whale | orca | *also called
